Backport of upstream commit 346aa974256a3df3e77ed9516a3775c809f7d05e
(PR https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/7892,
 GHSA-fjqc-hq36-qh5p, CVE-2026-48775) for langgraph-checkpoint 4.0.1.

Restricts lc:2 JSON envelope revival in JsonPlusSerializer to the default
constructor; the `method` field is now ignored. This removes the
attacker-controlled getattr(cls, method) dispatch that allowed pivoting a
safe pydantic class (e.g. AIMessage) to parse_raw(..., allow_pickle=True)
and reaching pickle.loads. A logger.warning is emitted when the default
constructor raises so legacy payloads that previously fell back to
construct(**kwargs) are observable instead of silently degrading.

The unused _encode_constructor_args helper is also removed; the framework's
own encoder has not emitted method= since the msgpack migration, and the
only legacy emission was method=(None, "construct") for pydantic models,
where the first entry (None) already meant "default constructor" -- which
is what the new code does unconditionally.

Semantic backport notes (4.0.1 vs upstream 4.1.x):
  * Target lacks _is_safe_json_type / _warned_unregistered_types /
    _warned_blocked_types / _warn_once / Reviver(allowed_objects="core") /
    _DeltaSnapshot. None are required for the security-relevant change.
  * Tests that depended on the upstream safe-type bypass (which lets
    LangChain SAFE types revive without an explicit allowlist) are adapted
    to pass an explicit allowed_json_modules=[("langchain_core.messages.ai",
    "AIMessage")] so they exercise the same security property on 4.0.1.

